{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And he said, for a hand is upon the throne of Yah.</b> 'And he said' refers back to Moses. 'For a hand' — thus is the way of one who swears, to place his hand upon an object, and it is a figure of speech, like the language of (Deuteronomy 32:40) ״כי אשא אל שמים ידי״, (Numbers 14:30) ״אשר נשאתי את ידי״." "<b>And by way of</b> the plain sense (peshat): 'a hand upon the throne of Yah' means that HaShem — may He be exalted — adjures every king of Israel who sits upon the throne of royalty to wage war for HaShem against Amalek. This teaches that the war and the spoil are all forbidden for personal benefit, and everything is to be for HaShem, not for men. And because of this the punishment came upon Saul, from the generation of Saul until the generation of Mordecai. And Mordecai knew that Saul his forefather was punished with a great punishment, and his punishment was measure for measure, for Scripture made the perfection of the throne depend on the vengeance against Amalek, and he was not scrupulous in his vengeance; therefore he was punished that he lost the Name and the throne, for no name remained after him, but he and Jonathan his son were killed together, and the throne of his kingdom fell. And because of this Mordecai was scrupulous not to benefit from the spoil of Haman, who was of the seed of Amalek, as it is written concerning the downfall of Haman (Esther 9:10): ״ובבזה לא שלחו את ידם״ — and in the spoil they did not stretch out their hand — because the Torah had warned concerning this (Deuteronomy 25:19): ״תמחה את זכר עמלק״. And so we find regarding the future, the war and the spoil are all for HaShem, as it is said (Micah 4:13): ״והחרמתי לה' בצעם וחילם לאדון כל הארץ״." "<b>And by way of</b> the Midrash: 'a hand upon the throne of Yah' — it did not say 'the throne of YHWH.' The Holy One, blessed be He, swore that the throne is not whole and the Name is not whole until He takes vengeance on the seed of Amalek. By way of the Kabbalah the matter of this Midrash will be explained in this manner." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: 'a hand upon the throne of Yah' — this hand is 'a war for HaShem,' which is the attribute of Judgment above. And Scripture reveals to you that it is 'upon the throne of Yah,' for the name Yah is the attribute of Judgment below, as it is written (Exodus 15:2): ״עזי וזמרת יה״, as I explained in its place. Therefore it says that the hand which is upon the throne of Yah, which is 'a war for HaShem,' shall be 'a war against Amalek from generation to generation,' for it will punish him with the attribute from above, which is the attribute of harsh Judgment, in order to destroy him from this world and the world to come by cutting off his strength from him; and therefore it wages war against him because he cut it off from Him, and the Name and the throne remained as though deficient. And the explanation of the Midrash — 'the Name and the throne' — is that they are the seven attributes alluded to in the letters vav-he, which are a throne for what is above. Or one may say, 'a hand upon the throne of Yah' — for Amalek stretched his hand upon the throne of Yah, that is, upon the vav-he which are a throne for the yod-he, which are the three first ones, as you know; and therefore, 'a war for HaShem against Amalek from generation to generation.' In my opinion, this is the secret of the verse that we find in Esau: אלוף עלוה, and in Chronicles (1 Chronicles 1:51) Moses himself wrote אלופים with a yod in order to complete the Name, as it is written (Psalms 2): ״על ה' ועל משיחו״. And further, the word כס alludes to the clouds that surround the throne, which are seven, from what is written (Job 26): פרשז with the addition of the letter zayin. And when Israel do the will of the Place, the clouds open in the shape of a kaf, and when they do not do the will of the Place, they close in the shape of a samekh, as it is written (Lamentations 3:44): ״סכותה בענן״, and this is (Exodus 24:15): ״ויכס הענן את ההר״, (ibid. 40): ״ויכס הענן את אהל מועד״. And you already know that there were seven clouds for Israel in the wilderness." "<b>And I saw</b> from one of the kabbalists who wrote concerning this: Know and understand that the Throne of Glory channels blessing and power to the seventy angels that surround the throne, who are appointed over the seventy nations, and they are princes over them, governing them. And Amalek was of the seed of Esau, and therefore his power was great and mighty, for the power of Esau his forefather was sustained and blessed from the power of Isaac, which is the attribute of Gevurah, and this matter is alluded to in the word ויחלש — it did not say ויהרג but ויחלש, that is to say, he weakened the great power above that draws strength from the attribute of Gevurah and severed it from there, so that they would fall before him by the sword. Now Amalek is one of the seventy nations, and his power is one of the seventy princes, and when this Amalek sinned, HaShem — may He be exalted — cut off his power from the throne, so that he would not be sustained from it and would not draw power of blessing from within the innermost, but only from the power of the stars and constellations. And the cutting off of his power from the throne is the oath here, where it says 'a hand upon the throne of Yah.' And the matter is as though the throne were deficient and the Name deficient, for when He withdraws His power from the throne, the throne appears deficient and also the Name appears deficient — it appears as though He does not sustain everything and there is another power besides Him, Heaven forbid. And therefore the alef is missing from כסא, for His primordial power was withdrawn from the throne on account of Amalek, and likewise the vav and the he from the Name. But in the days of the Messiah, when HaShem — may He be exalted — visits upon the host of heaven and abolishes the supernal appointees from their posts, as it is written in Daniel (Daniel 8:10): ״ותגדל עד צבא השמים ותפל ארצה מן הצבא ומן הכוכבים ותרמסם״ — the nations will perish with ease through the destruction of the princes appointed over them. And many of the nations will return to our faith, as it is written (Zechariah 8:23): ״יחזיקו עשרה אנשים״ and so on, and it is written (Zephaniah 3:9): ״כי אז אהפוך אל עמים שפה ברורה לקרא כלם בשם ה' לעבדו שכם אחד״ — and there is no nation in the world that does not have a portion in the Holy One, blessed be He. But Amalek and Esau will have no portion or remembrance among the rest of the nations that remain, as it is written (Obadiah 1:18): ״ולא יהיה שריד לבית עשו״ — this explains the verse, that of the rest of the gentiles there will be survivors and fugitives who remain from them to serve HaShem, but of the seed of Esau there is none; rather they will be blotted out from the world, as it is written: ״כי מחה אמחה את זכר עמלק״. And then the Name and the throne will be upon their perfection, for the three letters, namely alef, he, and vav, are the completion of the throne and the Name. And of this David said, peace be upon him (Psalms 132:13): ״כי בחר ה' בציון אוה למושב לו״ — it says that in the future, when the Holy One, blessed be He, chooses Zion, then He will sit upon a whole throne, and this is the language of אוה, which is the completion of the throne and the Name. And likewise David said, peace be upon him (Psalms 9:6): ״האויב תמו חרבות לנצח וערים נתשת אבד זכרם המה״, and it is written: ״וה' לעולם ישב כונן למשפט כסאו״ — ״וה' לעולם ישב״, behold the Name is whole; ״כונן למשפט כסאו״, behold the throne is whole. And then the dominion will be to HaShem — may He be exalted — alone, as it is said (Isaiah 2:11): ״ונשגב ה' לבדו ביום ההוא״, and it is written (Obadiah 1:21): ״ועלו מושיעים בהר ציון לשפוט את הר עשו והיתה לה' המלוכה״, and ״והיה ה' למלך על כל הארץ ביום ההוא יהיה ה' אחד ושמו אחד״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {3 "The citation of Job 26 for the word פרשז appears to refer to Job 26:9 (פרשז according to some readings); the verse reference is left as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:00:58.109271980Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}